      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To assess community-level volatility in rapidly transitioning neighborhoods, focus on indicators related to socio-economic equilibrium. Track housing affordability metrics, such as rent-to-income ratios, as sudden spikes can signal market stress. Monitor local changes in demographic composition alongside utilization rates of public services to gauge strain on existing infrastructure. Finally, track business formation and closure rates to see if local economic stability is keeping pace with population influx.",
